id: interface/yawn-temporal-header-v0.1
title: "Yawn temporal identity, replay, and provisioning header"
kind: interface-boundary-contract
status: proposed-0.1
updated: 2026-09-04

purpose: >
  Make a Yawn's stable identity, current temporal position, replay affordance,
  and effective provisioning visible at the same place the user sees the Yawn's
  icon, title, and address. Time is not decorative metadata: a Yawn is a
  time-indexed orientation contract whose meaning, evidence, authority, and
  relationships can change across authorized events.

header_identity:
  required_visible:
    - yawn_icon_or_fallback
    - yawn_title
    - canonical_or_resolved_address
    - current_effective_timestamp
    - effective_provisioning_summary
  interaction:
    timestamp: "opens the temporal replay aperture"
    provisioning: "opens the effective sharing/provisioning aperture"

replay_view:
  controls:
    - play_forward
    - pause
    - play_reverse
    - scrub
    - select_moment
  source_rule: >
    Replay moments must derive from preserved, attributable Yawn events,
    revisions, receipts, or authorized snapshots. UI animation is not proof and
    must never synthesize historical semantic state that was not actually
    recorded.
  selected_moment_rule: >
    Selecting a historical moment changes the View/aperture only. It does not
    roll back, mutate, authorize, or replace current canonical state.
  current_marker: >
    Returning to the latest moment returns the user to the current replay head.

clock_semantics:
  preferred_timestamp: "latest authorized semantic event effective_time"
  acceptable_fallback: "record updated_at when no semantic replay head is available"
  requirement: >
    The interface should distinguish a semantic/effective event timestamp from a
    storage-write timestamp when both are available. Ordering must be
    deterministic and preserve source timestamps and provenance.

provisioning_view:
  compact_states:
    - private
    - shared
    - public
  requirements:
    - "The compact state is visible without opening settings."
    - "Shared state may expose a count or safe summary without leaking recipient identities."
    - "Inherited provisioning is visibly distinguishable from an explicit local decision."
    - "Provisioning is independent from epistemic confidence, truth, or authority."
  replay_access_rule: >
    Historical replay must never widen access because a past snapshot had a
    broader provisioning state. Access to historical content is bounded by the
    intersection of the viewer's current rights and the historical record's
    permitted visibility, subject to explicit rightful grants.

view_boundaries:
  - "Timestamp is not freshness of truth; it is a temporal coordinate."
  - "Replay is a View over preserved history, not destructive version switching."
  - "Provisioning is not ownership, truth, endorsement, or authority."
  - "Public/private badges must not encode semantics only by color."
  - "Every replayed rendered object resolves to stable canonical identity."
  - "Historical claims retain the actor, epistemic status, evidence, and authority they had at that moment."
  - "A later update does not erase a prior disagreement or source record."

product_language:
  current: "Last updated"
  deeper_meaning: >
    The timestamp is a doorway into the Yawn's lived history: what changed,
    when it changed, who or what changed it, what was believed or authorized at
    that moment, and what proof later revised it.

implementation_notes:
  progressive_delivery:
    phase_1: >
      Surface icon, title, address, latest recorded timestamp, and provisioning.
      If only one replay moment exists, show disabled replay controls honestly.
    phase_2: >
      Bind replay controls to the canonical replay/event source and materialize
      historical Views by event position.
    phase_3: >
      Add diffs between moments, relationship/proof changes, and relevance-aware
      jumps to meaningful history without making every storage write a cognitive
      event.

links:
  - core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
  - core/holarchy.yawn
  - core/turn.yawn
  - core/orientation.yawn
  - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn

proof_conditions:
  - "A Yawn header visibly presents icon, title, address, timestamp, and provisioning."
  - "Clicking the timestamp exposes play, pause, reverse, and scrub controls."
  - "A one-moment Yawn never pretends a fabricated replay history exists."
  - "Selecting history changes only the View until an explicit separate mutation is authorized."
  - "Private/shared/public state is readable without relying on color alone."
  - "Current access rights cannot be widened by replaying a historically broader snapshot."
